tanding context. It is loaded on every UI edit and\nneeded only during a story sweep. It also already points at\n`.claude/rules/stories.md` for \"the full authoring conventions\" — a second home\nthat makes the duplication explicit.\n\n## Findings\n\n**F1 — Heading drift in `apps/api/AGENTS.md`.** The 442-line section\n`## Local database & RLS (dev)` contains six unrelated topics. Only the first\n441 tokens are about the local database.\n\n| Lines | Actual topic | ~tok | Normative owner already exists |\n| --- | --- | ---: | --- |\n| 145–171 | dev DB setup | 441 | — (keep) |\n| 172–230 | providers/models config-as-code | 1,021 | `openspec/specs/instance-config` (59.8k) |\n| 231–350 | Handlebars prompt templating | 2,093 | `openspec/specs/model-system-prompts` (43.9k) |\n| 351–473 | context-injection rail | 1,963 | `openspec/specs/context-injection` (28.8k) |\n| 474–521 | memory consent + recency digest | 821 | `openspec/specs/memory`, `chat-recency-digest` (42.6k) |\n| 522–586 | `app_rls` BYPASSRLS provisioning | 1,093 | — (belongs in `src/db`) |\n\n**F2 — The migration exception ledger is a drifting duplicate.** Lines 704–725\nare 5,044 tokens describing 22 hand-authored migrations. The `.sql` files\nalready carry this rationale in header comments, and they carry it *better*:\n`20260823083954_embedding_report_function.sql` explains the\n`CREATE OR REPLACE`/ownership hazard in 14 header lines that read more clearly\nthan the AGENTS.md sentence which merely gestures at them (\"the migration's own\nheader is explicit that…\"). Two copies of one fact, one of which is not next to\nthe code.\n\nVerified safe to consolidate: `drizzle-orm@0.45.2`'s `migrate()`\n(`pg-core/dialect.js:44`) gates purely on `created_at < migration.folderMillis`.\nThe SHA-256 it computes is **inserted, never compared** — editing comments in an\nalready-applied `.sql` cannot break an existing database.\n\nBehind the 22 named exceptions there are only four recurring patterns:\nhand-appended `FORCE